<title>USA: Honda prices 1997 Prelude.</title>
<headline>Honda prices 1997 Prelude.</headline>
<dateline>TORRANCE, Calif. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honda Motor Co Ltd's American Honda Motor Co Inc said Tuesday the 1997 Honda Prelude will be priced from $23,200 to $25,700.  </p>
<p>The car, which will arrive at dealers this week, comes in two models, a Prelude and a Prelude Type SH, American Honda said.</p>
<p>The lower-priced model includes a 2.2-liter, 16-valve, aluminum alloy engine with variable valve timing and lift electronic control (VTEC). The lowest priced 1996 Prelude with the VTEC engine was $25,880, Honda said.</p>
<p>The Type SH model includes an active torque transfer system for enhanced handling, Honda said.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
